From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:27:28 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Meridian: OpenCode answers Ask with the person's model;
 Connect adds --text-only for a model without images

- Ask: `opencode run` without -m doesn't take the model picked in OpenCode's
  own screen (state/opencode/model.json); it takes its first available one,
  signed out a free one ("Free usage limit reached"). Meridian now names
  the person's model: "model" of the global config files (JSONC; the later
  file wins), else the one last picked in OpenCode. Never one it made up;
  with none and OpenCode's free limit reached, Ask says so plainly.
- Connect (OpenCode): when that model is one of an @ai-sdk/openai-compatible
  provider set up in the config without image input (as OpenCode reads it,
  1 and 2), the bridge entry gets --text-only. Unsure: as before.
- ai::OpenCodeChosenModel, ai::OpenCodeModelTakesNoImages,
  OpenCodeWantsTextOnly (unit-tested).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
